adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the decrypted payload is handled as:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

There is no `try/catch` around `symmetricDecrypt` or `JSON.parse`, so any decryption failure or non-JSON plaintext will throw and bubble up as an unhandled exception (500). Also, the resulting `keys` object is written directly into `prisma.credential.update/create` as `key: keys` with no schema validation against the expected credential shape for the given `appSlug`/`appMetadata.type`, so an arbitrary (but validly decrypted) JSON blob can corrupt `credential.key`. Both behaviors are directly shown in the diff.
